53.Rule 7 of the Utilization of Surplus Funds Rules, 1960, speaks about Restrictions on Appropriation, which reads as under:
(a) Surplus may be appropriated only for:
(i) Section 66(i) purposes (religious/charitable/educational);
(ii) Section 36-A purposes (Hindu marriages of poor Hindus);
